---
// Install, check and remove coding.sh. The install script is the repo root's
// install.sh (served at /install); its options are read from that file. The
// outputs are from a packed build on a temp home.
import DocsLayout from "../../components/docs/DocsLayout.astro";
import Code from "../../components/docs/Code.astro";
import CodeTabs from "../../components/docs/CodeTabs.astro";
import Terminal from "../../components/Terminal.astro";
import { SOURCE_STEPS, INSTALL_SH } from "../../data/site";

const install = [
  { label: "Script", title: "shell", code: INSTALL_SH },
  { label: "npm", title: "shell", code: "npm install -g coding.sh\ncoding.sh init" },
  { label: "npx", title: "shell", code: "npx coding.sh init" },
];
const noPrompt = `curl -fsSL https://coding.sh/install | CODING_SH_YES=1 CODING_SH_NO_UI=1 sh`;
const source = `${SOURCE_STEPS[0]} && cd coding.sh
npm install && npm run build -w coding.sh
npm install -g ./packages/coding.sh   # puts coding.sh on your PATH, linked to this checkout
coding.sh init`;

const DOCTOR = `$ coding.sh doctor
  Checking agents…
✓ Claude Code     installed, hooked in ~/.claude/settings.json, no events yet
! Codex CLI       v0.167.0, hooked but not firing, no events yet
…
✓ Hook            ~/.coding.sh/bin/hook.mjs
✓ Spool           ~/.coding.sh/spool writable
✓ Store           sqlite sqlite://~/.coding.sh/index.db
…`;
const esc = (s: string) => s.replace(/&/g, "&amp;").replace(/</g, "&lt;").replace(/>/g, "&gt;");
const term = (s: string) =>
  s
    .split("\n")
    .map((l) => (l.startsWith("$ ") ? `<span class="t-muted">$</span> <span class="t-text">${esc(l.slice(2))}</span>` : esc(l)))
    .join("\n");

const remove = `coding.sh uninstall --dry-run   # show what would change
coding.sh uninstall --yes       # remove the hooks and MCP entries from every agent
npm uninstall -g coding.sh      # remove the CLI
rm -rf ~/.coding.sh             # optional: delete your recorded sessions too`;
---

<DocsLayout>
  <CodeTabs group="install" tabs={install} />
  <p>
    The script checks for Node 22.15 or newer and installs coding.sh from npm. If npm does not have the release or can't be reached, it takes the tarball from
    the GitHub release instead. Then it runs <code>coding.sh init</code>, which finds your agents, shows one plan and asks once before it
    writes anything. Last, it opens the viewer. Read the script at <a href="/install">coding.sh/install</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>npx coding.sh init</code> works too. The MCP server it registers then runs from the npx cache, so install globally if you want it
    to survive <code>npm cache clean</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="options">Script options</h2>
  <p>Set these on the <code>sh</code> side of the pipe:</p>
  <Code code={noPrompt} />
  <div class="doc-table">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>CODING_SH_VERSION</code></td><td>Install this release instead of the latest. Give its tag, as listed on the GitHub releases page.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CODING_SH_TARBALL</code></td><td>Install this tarball, a path or a URL: a mirror, a machine without internet, or a build you packed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CODING_SH_SOURCE</code></td><td><code>npm</code> or <code>github</code>: install from that source only. By default npm comes first.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CODING_SH_YES=1</code></td><td>Run <code>init --yes</code>, with no prompt.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CODING_SH_NO_INIT=1</code></td><td>Install only. Run <code>coding.sh init</code> later.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>CODING_SH_NO_UI=1</code></td><td>Don't open the viewer at the end.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Without a terminal (an agent's shell, CI), the script installs only and prints the next command, unless <code>CODING_SH_YES=1</code> is set.</p>

  <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Node.js 22.15 or newer.</strong> coding.sh uses the SQLite and zstd built into Node, so nothing native is compiled.</li>
    <li><strong>git</strong>, for the repository snapshots that <code>coding.sh run</code> and repo-replay evals take.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Windows:</strong> run the script from Git Bash, which comes with <a href="https://gitforwindows.org">Git for Windows</a>. Eval
      commands need its <code>sh</code> too. Under WSL, coding.sh works as it does on Linux.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="check">Check the install</h2>
  <p>
    <code>coding.sh doctor</code> checks each agent it finds, whether its hooks are in place and firing, and whether the spool and the store
    are writable. A row marked <code>!</code> is a warning, with the command that fixes it.
  </p>
  <Terminal title="shell" label="Output of coding.sh doctor"><pre set:html={term(DOCTOR)} /></Terminal>
  <p>
    Here Codex is waiting for you to approve its hooks with <code>/hooks</code>. Add <code>--json</code> for one machine-readable document.
  </p>

  <h2 id="updates">Update</h2>
  <p>
    <code>coding.sh update</code> installs the latest release. Commands print one line when a newer release is out. That check runs in the
    background at most once a day; <code>CODING_SH_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1</code> turns it off.
  </p>

  <h2 id="data">Where your data lives</h2>
  <p>
    Everything is in <code>~/.coding.sh</code>. Set <code>CODING_SH_HOME</code> to keep it somewhere else. To turn recording off for one
    agent process, set <code>CODING_SH_DISABLE=1</code> in its environment. <a href="/docs/storage">Storage</a> lists what each file holds.
  </p>

  <h2 id="uninstall">Uninstall</h2>
  <Code code={remove} />
  <p>
    <code>uninstall</code> restores each agent config file as it was before <code>init</code>, if nothing else has edited it since. Otherwise
    it removes only the coding.sh entries. Your recorded sessions stay until you delete <code>~/.coding.sh</code>.
  </p>

  <details class="more" id="source">
    <summary>Install from source</summary>
    <p>To run the code on the main branch, or to work on coding.sh:</p>
    <Code title="build from source" code={source} />
    <p>Or skip the global install and run <code>node packages/coding.sh/dist/cli.mjs</code> from the checkout.</p>
  </details>
</DocsLayout>
